{"title":"Diameter","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><table style=\"border:thin solid black;padding:5px;float:right;margin:10px;\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"border:thin solid gray;\">\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/3/b93e62ca8e3b80b26714b654f32b62488bb1f155.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]unitsize(40pt);draw(unitcircle,black);pair O = (0,0);pair A = (-1,0);pair B = (1,0);draw(A--O--B);label(&quot;$O$&quot;,O,S);label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,W);label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,E);[/asy]\" width=\"182\" height=\"135\" />\t\n</p>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><div class=\"magnify\" style=\"float: right;\">\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Enlarge.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/5/58/Enlarge.png/15px-Enlarge.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"15\" height=\"9\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/5/58/Enlarge.png/23px-Enlarge.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/5/58/Enlarge.png/30px-Enlarge.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure></div> This circle has diameter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /><br />since center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lies on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />.\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>A <b>diameter</b> of a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Circle\" title=\"Circle\">circle</a> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Chord\" title=\"Chord\">chord</a> of that circle which passes through the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Center\" title=\"Center\">center</a>.  Thus a diameter divides the circle into two regions of equal <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Area\" title=\"Area\">area</a> called <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Semicircle\" title=\"Semicircle\">semicircles</a>.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Diameter_of_a_set\">Diameter of a set</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Diameter&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Diameter of a set\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The diameter of more general <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Set\" title=\"Set\">sets</a> can also be defined.  In any given <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Metric_space\" title=\"Metric space\">metric space</a> (that is, anywhere you can measure <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Distance\" title=\"Distance\">distances</a> between <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Point\" title=\"Point\">points</a> such as normal Euclidean 3-D space, the surface of the Earth, or any <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Real_number\" title=\"Real number\">real</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Vector_space\" title=\"Vector space\">vector space</a>) the diameter of a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Bounded\" title=\"Bounded\">bounded</a> set of points is the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Supremum\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Supremum\">supremum</a> of the distances between pairs of points.  In the case where the set of points is a circle, the diameter is the length of the diameter of the circle.\n</p><p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Diameter&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018082516\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.024 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.049 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 37/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 658/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 186/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 853/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   14.082      1 -total\n 49.99%    7.039      1 Template:Stub\n 47.59%    6.702      1 Template:Asy_image\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:3870:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018082516 and revision id 240301. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}